Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?taskmanager:=20Add=20"Edit=20Application?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=A6"=20to=20the=20context=20menu?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Task Manager offers no way to change how an app appears on it.
Kickoff and Kicker already have "Edit Application…", which opens the
menu editor on that entry; add the same action to the "More" submenu
for any task whose launcher URL resolves to an application with a menu
entry, and hide it when the panel is system immutable.

Pinned launchers had no "More" submenu; it now appears for them when
the application can be edited, showing only this action, since the
window actions in it do not apply to launchers.

BUG: 369167
---
 applets/taskmanager/backend.cpp         | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 applets/taskmanager/backend.h           |  3 ++
 applets/taskmanager/qml/ContextMenu.qml | 38 +++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 83 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/applets/taskmanager/backend.cpp b/applets/taskmanager/backend.cpp
index 1005d2a981..52258d6467 100644
--- a/applets/taskmanager/backend.cpp
+++ b/applets/taskmanager/backend.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@

 #include <KApplicationTrader>
 #include <KIO/ApplicationLauncherJob>
